      "quality": "poor",
      "qualityReason": "location_description"
    },
    {
      "id": 2,
      "text": "The town was known as New Diana until the late 1990s, a name that reflected its post‑oil boom identity.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        17,
        18
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Wikipedia"
      ],
      "source": "https://en.wikipedia.org/wiki/Diana%2C_Texas",
      "category": "etymology",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 3,
      "text": "Oil discovered three miles south of the original town in the 1930s sparked the founding of New Diana, which grew into the modern community of Diana.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        27
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/diana-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 4,
      "text": "By the mid‑1960s, Diana boasted two churches, a school, and three or four stores, reflecting its steady post‑war growth.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        29
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/diana-tx",
      "category": "history",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 5,
      "text": "In 1990, Diana served as a commercial hub for surrounding farmers and ranchers, supporting a dozen or so businesses.",
      "sourceSentenceIds": [
        30
      ],
      "sourceLabels": [
        "Web source 1"
      ],
      "source": "https://www.tshaonline.org/handbook/entries/diana-tx",
      "category": "economy",
      "quality": "good"
    },
    {
      "id": 6,
      "text": "The mascot of New Diana Independent School District is the Eagle, a symbol embraced by students and the community alike.",
